   "date": "2026-11-02T05:49:13Z",
   "email": "329969015+margin-agents[bot]@users.noreply.github.com",
   "message": "sample 2026-11-02T05:49Z"
  },
  {
   "sha": "4f86f88856bda34aa2fcb26ebda1fb9b6f5bfb6b",
   "html_url": "https://github.com/SebR214/margin/commit/4f86f88856bda34aa2fcb26ebda1fb9b6f5bfb6b",
   "date": "2026-11-02T05:30:40Z",
   "email": "329969015+margin-agents[bot]@users.noreply.github.com",
   "message": "sample 2026-11-02T05:30Z"
  },
  {
   "sha": "f72b14a6b73527966c2b4d3344b92eb35ed04f8a",
   "html_url": "https://github.com/SebR214/margin/commit/f72b14a6b73527966c2b4d3344b92eb35ed04f8a",
   "date": "2026-11-02T05:22:37Z",
   "email": "person",
   "message": "SEB-301: the watchdogs email Seb through healthchecks.io (#776)\n\nGitHub's failure email goes to whoever triggered a run. The watchdog runs are\ndispatched by github-actions[bot], so every red run since 02:30 UTC on 2 Nov\nemailed nobody. Both watchdogs now ping a healthchecks.io check each run (up,\nor /fail with the reason). It emails on down, on recovery, and when pings stop\narriving, which also catches a dead chain. A missing ping URL fails the run.\n\nCo-authored-by: Sebastian Roervig <sebastian.roervig@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
  },
  {
   "sha": "036f485ef9598ef89e369fbfd6f0134e21c8b10d",
   "html_url": "https://github.com/SebR214/margin/commit/036f485ef9598ef89e369fbfd6f0134e21c8b10d",
   "date": "2026-11-02T05:18:40Z",
   "email": "person",
   "message": "SEB-301: the number audit skips venues in quarantine, as the index does (#775)\n\ncountry:SGD (and MXN) failed the watchdog since 02:30 UTC on 2 Nov: the audit\ncounted OKX spot (SGD), a quarantined second venue, as a second order book,\nwhile the published number is correctly one venue. Same rule as\nemit_countries: only an approved source is re-derived.\n\nCo-authored-by: Sebastian Roervig <sebastian.roervig@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
  },
